{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347891-when-should-npcs-launch-decisives","id":1347891,"title":"When Should NPCs Launch Decisives?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-12T07:38:30-08:00","id":1347891,"title":"When Should NPCs Launch Decisives?","content":"Basically I was trying to think at what initiative should the antagonists be trying to fire off decisive attacks? If they\u2019re just trying to deal lasting damage than almost any time they\u2019re over the enemy hardness is good. They might die faster but they\u2019ll take a chunk with them. Should they wait until there\u2019s a t least a reasonable chance that they\u2019ll knock out a player, even if that chance is never likely to happen? Do animals that don\u2019t realize Exalted may be more hardy fight as though 7 health levels will be a killshot?<br /> <br /> When I\u2019ve ST\u2019d I\u2019ve almost exclusively used the strategy that enemies don\u2019t launch decisive attacks unless they have a pretty good chance of taking a foe out of the fight, but maybe that\u2019s not the best way. There are even a few enemies that seem like they might really want to open up the start of the fight with a decisive attack. Is that unfair to the players because I have an endless supply of enemies and they don\u2019t have an endless supply of health levels, or is it intentional because it\u2019s ultimately not that deadly but does add to the drama as intense and dangerous places build up some temporary battle damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T07:53:55-08:00","id":1347897,"title":"","content":"It depends on how informed the NPCs are, but I'd have them launch decisives when they are about 10-14 initiative. Enough to almost guarantee dealing some lethal damage.<br /> <br /> Nobody wants to play rocket tag again, where the first to land a decisive splats their enemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T07:58:29-08:00","id":1347898,"title":"","content":"I think NPCs using Decisives on turn 1 is part of the game and comes with ups alongside the downs. In some cases it will hurt, but in other cases a pouncing tiger might waste their whole ini pool against a PC with hardness before they realize their mistake.<br /> <br /> Also group composition matters, if your whole PC circle has 6 hardness between the 5 of them then you may want to space out those 1st turn decisives a little, whereas if there is a bodyguard specialized Melee character you'll want to go all out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T07:58:54-08:00","id":1347899,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's a clear answer to this other than &quot;what feels right for you.&quot; I've had several combat situations in recent story arcs where the PCs have been in very good positions and often kept the bad guys at low initiative enough for the bad guys to only rarely get a chance to do a decisive strike before they'll be locked down at low initiative or in crash. When I know that a fight is looking like it'll turn into that, I may want to do a decisive strike at lower initiative to put some pressure on the players. In a different situation when the fight looks worse for the PCs and they're the ones running low, I may want to crash one of them and have that big potential one shot kill instead of grazing blows mainly for the dramatic impact - to make the big bad look bigger and badder. I rarely put my players in situations that look like it'd TPK them, though, never actually having perma-killed a PC in a fight in 3E yet (though I've perma-crippled some of them).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T08:07:34-08:00","id":1347900,"title":"","content":"I think you are taking the the problem &quot;upside down&quot; (I don't know if that makes sense in this sentence I just watched Stranger Things and it seems to make sense).<br /> <br /> To me, Initiative is a strategical game for the player, and a representation of what's happening in the fight for the characters.<br /> <br /> When a character really damages another, it means the player launched a decisive attack. When he almost really damages another, it means it was a withering. For the characters, in both cases he was trying to damage his opponent. This is what's strictly written in the books.<br /> <br /> Now, my personal interpretation of this system is the following : For the players, Initiative is here to provide an actual &quot;mini-game&quot; to interact with, with strategical decisions and stuff, in order to have fun and abstract the fight. So if you consider your NPC doing a decisive attack is a good strategical play from the player or ST perspective, you should do it. The character doesn't realize he will expose himself after a decisive attack because he will only have 3 initiative left, neither does he realize than when he throws a 5 initiative decisive attack on someone with 10 hardness he will not damage him, it's the player who knows this information. From the perspective of the character, it's just the heat and surprise of the fight.<br /> <br /> It doesn't mean the character must do stupid actions because he has no meta-knowledge. For example, a character doesn't have to necessarily use a decisive attack when he has enough initiative if it should put him in a suicidal situation. It's the player behind the character that chooses the strategical option he decides to apply, and the initiative system then translates into the game world by incarnating luck, stupidity, wit, courage, passion, or anything else accordingly to the mood of the fight.<br /> <br /> My conclusion to your exact question is thus : If the narrative objective of the ST in a fight scene is to have his NPCs weaken the players and then die, he should follow this strategy for his NPC. It doesn't mean his NPC are suicidal, because from their perspective they are just fighting an enemy and putting all they have on the line. Only if in the context of the fight they are given a good reason to stop or change their plans (for example, they are terribly hurt, or they realize they become overwhelmed with malus because they are blinded and mauled, or the players do a well argumented social roll that uses the Social System effectively), they should maybe question changing plans, in accordance of the psychology the ST has given them. But for as long as the ST can use his optimal strategy, his NPCs should be the vector to apply it.<br /> <br /> Edit : Of course, the strategic choices of the Storyteller should be informed by what the characters have a chance to know. If her NPC never met the characters, he shouldn't know one of them has 10 hidden hardness thanks to a strange power. But if she sees a guy shining in full Orichalcum armor, then the ST can consider he possesses the strategical information that Big Shining Guy has hardness, and thus not use his character to attack him without enough initiative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":24291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","user":"Chausse","date":".  Edit : Precision 11-12-2019, 11:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T08:21:36-08:00","id":1347903,"title":"","content":"I'm almost the exact opposite.<br /> My NPCs frequently employ decisive attacks against my PCs when they could be building initiative so that I minimise the risk of potential killshots and create windows for another PC to intervine with a Defend Other action if one of them is clearly struggling.<br /> <br /> On the other side of things, I only expect most NPCs to get lucky once if at all. I don't want to waste that on accumulating initiative that they won't live long enough to use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 11-12-2019, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T08:31:36-08:00","id":1347906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347891-when-should-npcs-launch-decisives?p=1347900#post1347900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you are taking the the problem &quot;upside down&quot; (I don't know if that makes sense in this sentence I just watched Stranger Things and it seems to make sense).<br /> <br /> To me, Initiative is a strategical game for the player, and a representation of what's happening in the fight for the characters.<br /> <br /> When a character really damages another, it means the player launched a decisive attack. When he almost really damages another, it means it was a withering. For the characters, in both cases he was trying to damage his opponent. This is what's strictly written in the books.<br /> <br /> Now, my personal interpretation of this system is the following : For the players, Initiative is here to provide an actual &quot;mini-game&quot; to interact with, with strategical decisions and stuff, in order to have fun and abstract the fight. So if you consider your NPC doing a decisive attack is a good strategical play from the player or ST perspective, you should do it. The character doesn't realize he will expose himself after a decisive attack because he will only have 3 initiative left, neither does he realize than when he throws a 5 initiative decisive attack on someone with 10 hardness he will not damage him, it's the player who knows this information. From the perspective of the character, it's just the heat and surprise of the fight.<br /> <br /> It doesn't mean the character must do stupid actions because he has no meta-knowledge. For example, a character doesn't have to necessarily use a decisive attack when he has enough initiative if it should put him in a suicidal situation. It's the player behind the character that chooses the strategical option he decides to apply, and the initiative system then translates into the game world by incarnating luck, stupidity, wit, courage, passion, or anything else accordingly to the mood of the fight.<br /> <br /> My conclusion to your exact question is thus : If the narrative objective of the ST in a fight scene is to have his NPCs weaken the players and then die, he should follow this strategy for his NPC. It doesn't mean his NPC are suicidal, because from their perspective they are just fighting an enemy and putting all they have on the line. Only if in the context of the fight they are given a good reason to stop or change their plans (for example, they are terribly hurt, or they realize they become overwhelmed with malus because they are blinded and mauled, or the players do a well argumented social roll that uses the Social System effectively), they should maybe question changing plans, in accordance of the psychology the ST has given them. But for as long as the ST can use his optimal strategy, his NPCs should be the vector to apply it.<br /> <br /> Edit : Of course, the strategic choices of the Storyteller should be informed by what the characters have a chance to know. If her NPC never met the characters, he shouldn't know one of them has 10 hidden hardness thanks to a strange power. But if she sees a guy shining in full Orichalcum armor, then the ST can consider he possesses the strategical information that Big Shining Guy has hardness, and thus not use his character to attack him without enough initiative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Entirely fair.<br /> <br /> I would suggest that NPCs can understand initiative a little bit, in that when they are at low(&lt;5) initiative they feel off balance and not in control, and at high(&gt;10) initiative they feel things are going their way and they're controlling the fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T08:32:58-08:00","id":1347907,"title":"","content":"I think 15i (less for obviously weaker or injured PCs), 10i when the NPC has any kind of Alpha Strike abilities, or when Crashing a PC is a good benchmark.<br /> <br /> It's not a guarenteed kill against a normal mortal, but it's a decisive advantage, especially pack hunters. It keeps the combat dynamic, passes on concequences. If you roll above average you're still unlikely to kill a PC.<br /> <br /> The combat system is mechanically transparent. I don't think it's particularly meta to use the salient knowledge the rules specifically impart you with. The meta system knowledge is the mechanical representation of how the characters perceive the flow of combat. You know if a character is Crashed, because in-character they <i>seem</i> on the ropes. You <i>choose</i> whether to launch a Decisive, not because you don't intend on killing your foe when you Wither, but because you choose not to overextend yourself to try to land that killing blow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-12-2019, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T08:50:54-08:00","id":1347914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347891-when-should-npcs-launch-decisives?p=1347907#post1347907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think 15i (less for obviously weaker or injured PCs), 10i when the NPC has any kind of Alpha Strike abilities, or when Crashing a PC is a good benchmark.<br /> <br /> It's not a guarenteed kill against a normal mortal, but it's a decisive advantage, especially pack hunters. It keeps the combat dynamic, passes on concequences. If you roll above average you're still unlikely to kill a PC.<br /> <br /> The combat system is mechanically transparent. I don't think it's particularly meta to use the salient knowledge the rules specifically impart you with. The meta system knowledge is the mechanical representation of how the characters perceive the flow of combat. You know if a character is Crashed, because in-character they <i>seem</i> on the ropes. You <i>choose</i> whether to launch a Decisive, not because you don't intend on killing your foe when you Wither, but because you choose not to overextend yourself to try to land that killing blow.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think we will argue with each other for long because we will hit a wall but I would strongly not suggest an interpretation where the character &quot;knows&quot; that after doing a decisive he is exposed in term of initiative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T08:59:43-08:00","id":1347916,"title":"","content":"I tend to fire off decisive attacks if the NPC has the initiative to do it. One because the players rarely allow npcs to even have initiative long enough to use it, and two throwing around low damage attacks adds more value to the smaller systems of the game. Ox-body shows its value, wound penalties subtly influence the pace of battle, healing starts to matter etc. Three seeing lots of smaller decisive attacks makes the big decisive attacks much more dramatic, players remember those times they got careless and an Exalt dropped a big attack on them, the crippling rules have saved a few characters at the cost of an arm or a leg.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T09:07:37-08:00","id":1347919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347891-when-should-npcs-launch-decisives?p=1347916#post1347916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to fire off decisive attacks if the NPC has the initiative to do it. One because the players rarely allow npcs to even have initiative long enough to use it, and two throwing around low damage attacks adds more value to the smaller systems of the game. Ox-body shows its value, wound penalties subtly influence the pace of battle, healing starts to matter etc. Three seeing lots of smaller decisive attacks makes the big decisive attacks much more dramatic, players remember those times they got careless and an Exalt dropped a big attack on them, the crippling rules have saved a few characters at the cost of an arm or a leg.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if homebrewing some sort of maximum initiative would stop players from trying to amass like 50i in order to oneshot an enemy Exalt instead of multiple decisives like the system intends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T09:16:02-08:00","id":1347922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347891-when-should-npcs-launch-decisives?p=1347919#post1347919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wonder if homebrewing some sort of maximum initiative would stop players from trying to amass like 50i in order to oneshot an enemy Exalt instead of multiple decisives like the system intends.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking about this as well, something like &quot;You can't withering if you already have X initiative&quot; but most players totally didn't want to do this. I found it kinda sad because it made some fights really long (My dawn player with 18 initiative launching a withering attack was just the lamest thing ever)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T09:24:37-08:00","id":1347924,"title":"","content":"I haven't really started running Ex3 yet, so take this with a grain of salt, but I'm in favor of the &quot;many small attacks&quot; approach. Everything seems to support that: Getting blown away in a single hit never feels good. Hardness matters. A battle where you take two levels of damage feels a lot more dangerous, in a way that trading initiative back and forth doesn't really do. It just... Feels right. My goal as GM is to make the players THINK they might die, not actually murder them.<br /> <br /> (At least not often)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T09:28:07-08:00","id":1347925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347891-when-should-npcs-launch-decisives?p=1347922#post1347922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking about this as well, something like &quot;You can't withering if you already have X initiative&quot; but most players totally didn't want to do this. I found it kinda sad because it made some fights really long (My dawn player with 18 initiative launching a withering attack was just the lamest thing ever)</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't thinking that you can't perform withering attacks, but that once you get to X initiative, gaining anything further simply vanishes. There'd still be value in trying to crash your opponent, so they couldn't defend very well against your max initiative decisive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T09:37:59-08:00","id":1347929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347891-when-should-npcs-launch-decisives?p=1347900#post1347900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My conclusion to your exact question is thus : If the narrative objective of the ST in a fight scene is to have his NPCs weaken the players and then die, he should follow this strategy for his NPC.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'll also say that the system is supposed to be transparent, and I think it's fine for a tiger to not waste its initiative on an enemy with Hardness.<br /> Although that doesn't mean an ST should use their knowledge of PC's charms that they haven't actually used in the battle yet.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I wonder if homebrewing some sort of maximum initiative would stop players from trying to amass like 50i in order to oneshot an enemy Exalt instead of multiple decisives like the system intends.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this something many players do?<br /> <br /> Once my players have 15+ initiative, they normally make decisive attacks. Definitely at 20+. Otherwise it's pretty much a waste. I mean, even if you don't kill someone with a 20i attack, you're going to give them some pretty hefty wound penalties.<br /> Still, maybe this is because they rarely fight people with tons of ox-bodies and wound penalty negators, which I guess could change the tactics there.<br /> <br /> The only time I've ever seen more is when I kept hitting mortals to get to 48i before I attacked the Supernal-Resistance Dawn wearing full soulsteel plate armour (as I knew otherwise he'd just shrug it off).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <hr />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T09:40:54-08:00","id":1347930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347891-when-should-npcs-launch-decisives?p=1347929#post1347929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this something many players do?</div> </div> </div> </div>In my experience, yeah. They simply won't try to do any decisives until they've got 25-30i. They've always seemed to be afraid of dropping back down to 3i and eating a withering attack to crash them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T10:05:28-08:00","id":1347935,"title":"","content":"The difference between withering and decisive is diegetic. The character is always struggling to overpower, find openings and stab, and awareness of their own dominance in a battle relies transparently on both its pressure and the (pun intended) decisive wounds they managed to cause.<br /> <br /> So it's not a character decision, it's a player decision. Do it as much as you feel is narratively appropriate. Right after a crash is a scary moment where the decisive has extra tones of &quot;well, fuck&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 11-12-2019, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T10:13:45-08:00","id":1347938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347891-when-should-npcs-launch-decisives?p=1347925#post1347925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wasn't thinking that you can't perform withering attacks, but that once you get to X initiative, gaining anything further simply vanishes. There'd still be value in trying to crash your opponent, so they couldn't defend very well against your max initiative decisive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's really a matter of personal appreciation. <br /> <br /> If I want to home-brew something to dissuade players to take a course of action, then I do it fully. If I don't, I might still find some players searching for &quot;value in trying to crash your opponent, so they couldn't defend very well against your max initiative decisive&quot;, which is an optimal strategical decision that I fully understand, but then they are not engaging the dynamic and narrative aspect of the fight I'm trying to put forth by homebrewing.<br /> <br /> So it's your call basically, but if I have a player sitting at 25i still withering because he wants to &quot;make sure the other guy is crashed&quot;, well ... I'd be disappointed I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T10:15:59-08:00","id":1347940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347891-when-should-npcs-launch-decisives?p=1347929#post1347929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll also say that the system is supposed to be transparent, and I think it's fine for a tiger to not waste its initiative on an enemy with Hardness.<br /> Although that doesn't mean an ST should use their knowledge of PC's charms that they haven't actually used in the battle yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Charms are declared after the attack is declared I believe, so someone can surprise another with hidden Hardness Charms or power, but before that things like hardness or soak should be &quot;quite&quot; transparent when they are permanent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T10:18:05-08:00","id":1347942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347891-when-should-npcs-launch-decisives?p=1347900#post1347900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My conclusion to your exact question is thus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. That would certainly change things a lot. The beasts and devils of creation aren\u2019t fighting to win in the system, as in either victory or death, they\u2019re just fighting. A river dragon may just start the fight off with a decisive bite and go for the clinch straight away, then the rest of the battle takes place slamming the dragon around and prying its jaws apart to free the unlucky guy who got bit.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s not a strategy I would have used before because no river dragon starts combat with enough initiative to take out a character. Usually they won\u2019t get to act with that much either but if they spend some willpower on their stealth roll...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T10:39:37-08:00","id":1347951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347891-when-should-npcs-launch-decisives?p=1347938#post1347938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it's your call basically, but if I have a player sitting at 25i still withering because he wants to &quot;make sure the other guy is crashed&quot;, well ... I'd be disappointed I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>...that's not how it works. You can't keep someone in crash for longer than 3 turns. They will always reset to base after 3 turns, even if they've been driven to -50 initiative.<br /> <br /> Or just say the guy is dead or defeated, he's been beaten so bad that he can't even fight anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T10:47:47-08:00","id":1347956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347891-when-should-npcs-launch-decisives?p=1347951#post1347951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...that's not how it works. You can't keep someone in crash for longer than 3 turns. They will always reset to base after 3 turns, even if they've been driven to -50 initiative.<br /> <br /> Or just say the guy is dead or defeated, he's been beaten so bad that he can't even fight anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think in the example the PC has 25i but the NPC is <i>not</i> Crashed and the PC wants to Crash them before blowing all their Initative on a Decisive.<br /> <br /> (I'd encourage that line of thinking, personally.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T10:49:53-08:00","id":1347958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347891-when-should-npcs-launch-decisives?p=1347942#post1347942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting. That would certainly change things a lot. The beasts and devils of creation aren\u2019t fighting to win in the system, as in either victory or death, they\u2019re just fighting. A river dragon<br /> may just start the fight off with a decisive bite and go for the clinch straight away, then the rest of the battle takes place slamming the dragon around and prying its jaws apart to free the unlucky guy who got bit.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s not a strategy I would have used before because no river dragon starts combat with enough initiative to take out a character. Usually they won\u2019t get to act with that much either but if they spend some willpower on their stealth roll...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the idea is really to consider the options at your disposal from a strategic and meta point of view, and then chose the most optimal one. The only barrier should be &quot;Is this absurd from the situation inside the game from the perspective of the character ?&quot;. From your example, say your river-dragon (sorry I don't remember all their stats) is fighting the PCs. He got quite low on initiative so he will not finish an enemy, and everyone around him has high initiative, so they can threaten a kill on him.<ul><li>His first option would be to run away, because strategically you know he is gonna die, but it doesn't matter. If you put him here in the situation of an ambushing, it's clearly to die while fighting the PCs. From his in-game perspective, all he sees is that the preys are defending themselves, not that their &quot;damage level&quot; is red and ready to strike.</li> <li>His other option is to try a decisive attack against a random close enemy. It's more in line with your strategical objective as a ST, and it's a viable option to me.</li> <li>The even better option (in my eyes), because it's in line with your strategical objective and more dramatically engaging, is to try to grapple a player character and drag him in the closest river/lake to drown him (my translator suggested &quot;to walnut him&quot; I just can't stop laughing). It's certainly in line with his usual tactics in game (again, didn't read them recently, maybe it's not their thing at all it's just an example), with your strategical objective (put pressure on the PCs), and with the situation at hand (you don't have enough initiative to seriously threaten a player, for example).</li> </ul><br /> Once he has started dragging a player into the water, but he suddenly lost 3/4 of his hp because everyone else attacked him, it now starts to make sense for him to try to escape : It's written on the description of most animals that they will try to flee if they lose too much hp, and hp loss in an information the characters have conscience &quot;in game&quot; for the most part. So it's line with his psychology, and you should not make him &quot;continue the fight just to die&quot;, because at this point in the fight he has enough information to not do the absurd choice to stay and suicide for sure.<br /> <br /> Here would be my analysis of the kind of situation you suggested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T10:52:59-08:00","id":1347959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347891-when-should-npcs-launch-decisives?p=1347956#post1347956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think in the example the PC has 25i but the NPC is <i>not</i> Crashed and the PC wants to Crash them before blowing all their Initative on a Decisive.<br /> <br /> (I'd encourage that line of thinking, personally.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Chausse mentioned keeping them crashed, and that's what I was refuting.<br /> <br /> As for it being smart to crash an opponent first, I agree and I mentioned that myself. Chausse seems to feel that is unthematic or meta gaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T11:12:40-08:00","id":1347966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347891-when-should-npcs-launch-decisives?p=1347959#post1347959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Chausse mentioned keeping them crashed, and that's what I was refuting.<br /> <br /> As for it being smart to crash an opponent first, I agree and I mentioned that myself. Chausse seems to feel that is unthematic or meta gaming.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the part about crashing someone for more benefit I was being generic : If the other guy is not in crashed and you don't have 100% certainty to kill him, you could keep withering him to make sure he is crashed and maybe lose some special Perilous Charms. If he is already in Crash, you could keep withering him to make sure he will not make an Initiative Shift on you after a decisive attack. I mean, the strategical options are pretty numerous if you want to find good reasons to keep withering someone. <br /> <br /> As for the other point, it is obviously &quot;smart&quot; to crash an opponent first, I said already in many cases it has great chances of being the optimal play. But I think one of the ... particularity (I was going to say drawback but I think it's a matter of perspective) of the initiative system is going for the &quot;optimal&quot; or &quot;rational&quot; play can become pretty dull, precisely because optimal plays are not always the funs or dramatic ones. I feel it's unthematic because I was promised exciting reversals and unexpected development thanks to the initiative system, but arrived at a point where someone with 25i decides to keep withering, it rather becomes asthmatic pace and meaningless abstraction.<br /> <br /> I know I'm a bit hard on this one, I'm usually a rational player as well so if I see a logical play I will do it, but I feel at this point there is a misunderstanding between what the system is supposed to feel like and how the players use it. I don't blame it on the players making the rational choice, just wish it was a bit different (hence my home-brew proposals).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T11:21:16-08:00","id":1347970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347891-when-should-npcs-launch-decisives?p=1347966#post1347966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For the part about crashing someone for more benefit I was being generic : If the other guy is not in crashed and you don't have 100% certainty to kill him, you could keep withering him to make sure he is crashed and maybe lose some special Perilous Charms. If he is already in Crash, you could keep withering him to make sure he will not make an Initiative Shift on you after a decisive attack. I mean, the strategical options are pretty numerous if you want to find good reasons to keep withering someone.<br /> <br /> As for the other point, it is obviously &quot;smart&quot; to crash an opponent first, I said already in many cases it has great chances of being the optimal play. But I think one of the ... particularity (I was going to say drawback but I think it's a matter of perspective) of the initiative system is going for the &quot;optimal&quot; or &quot;rational&quot; play can become pretty dull, precisely because optimal plays are not always the funs or dramatic ones. I feel it's unthematic because I was promised exciting reversals and unexpected development thanks to the initiative system, but arrived at a point where someone with 25i decides to keep withering, it rather becomes asthmatic pace and meaningless abstraction.<br /> <br /> I know I'm a bit hard on this one, I'm usually a rational player as well so if I see a logical play I will do it, but I feel at this point there is a misunderstanding between what the system is supposed to feel like and how the players use it. I don't blame it on the players making the rational choice, just wish it was a bit different (hence my home-brew proposals).</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps a person can't maintain a dominating control of the fight and will reset to base-or lose a large chunk of initiative-if they stay at maximum initiative for 3 turns, just like someone in crash will reset.<br /> <br /> Or you can bring it up to the players about wanting to change they way they do battles. Exalted is all about the back and forth, not the massive splat after ten turns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T11:26:39-08:00","id":1347972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347891-when-should-npcs-launch-decisives?p=1347970#post1347970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps a person can't maintain a dominating control of the fight and will reset to base-or lose a large chunk of initiative-if they stay at maximum initiative for 3 turns, just like someone in crash will reset.<br /> <br /> Or you can bring it up to the players about wanting to change they way they do battles. Exalted is all about the back and forth, not the massive splat after ten turns.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry because I feel like we are basically on the same line &quot;I want my players not to stack a ton of initiative&quot;, but I feel like you are contesting me but I don't know on what point specifically. <br /> <br /> I think (a) &quot;Staying at max initiative for too many rounds will make you lose initiative&quot; is a solution to players stacking too much initiative, but I'm unsure if I prefer it to (b) &quot;You can't withering at max initiative&quot;. I think (b) is more elegant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T11:53:12-08:00","id":1347978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347891-when-should-npcs-launch-decisives?p=1347972#post1347972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think (a) &quot;Staying at max initiative for too many rounds will make you lose initiative&quot; is a solution to players stacking too much initiative, but I'm unsure if I prefer it to (b) &quot;You can't withering at max initiative&quot;. I think (b) is more elegant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of like the idea of max initiative as a complement to Crash-- the symmetry is appealing. Maybe something like &quot;When your Initiative is higher than 20, you enter Initiative Overflow. While in Overflow, you cannot gain more Initiative. Instead, you gain 1 wp for every 10 initiative you'd normally gain. If you make a Decisive Attack while in Overflow, you may reroll Join Battle to determine your new initiative afterwards, rather than resetting to the base of three.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T11:58:57-08:00","id":1347980,"title":"","content":"I'm unsure that adding strong benefits while at Max Initiative is something that will actually discourage players from stacking too much initiative <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T12:22:45-08:00","id":1347982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347891-when-should-npcs-launch-decisives?p=1347958#post1347958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the idea is really to consider the options at your disposal from a strategic and meta point of view, and then chose the most optimal one. The only barrier should be &amp;quot;Is this absurd from the situation inside the game from the perspective of the character ?&amp;quot;. From your example, say your river-dragon (sorry I don't remember all their stats) is fighting the PCs. He got quite low on initiative so he will not finish an enemy, and everyone around him has high initiative, so they can threaten a kill on him.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was more thinking from the perspective that river dragons have only 5 dice to their join battle, so they\u2019re only likely to get 5-6 initiative at the start of the fight, maybe more if they can somehow stunt it and spend some willpower or something. Normally that isn\u2019t really enough to do much, but river dragons have a cool ability when they deal 3+ levels of decisive damage they can reflexively grapple the target, which it makes unopposed, and gets some bonus initiative for the effort. It\u2019s a really neat ability, plus combined with Death Roll, which is a devastating double 7s decisive savage, it would add some real urgency to the battle, although unlikely to be much actual danger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T13:01:43-08:00","id":1347989,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah that seems really worth a shot indeed ! <br /> <br /> Should have went check my books to talk about that instead of rocketing through my thoughts, that'll teach me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T13:04:22-08:00","id":1347990,"title":"","content":"I had been revisiting the implications and strategies of when to go for Decisive Attacks recently as well, prompted by a comment in the other thread about a couple Buck-Ogres being more challenging if you are already at -2.<br /> <br /> At what point is the risk of suffering Initiative Shift worth the reward on completing a Decisive Attack against a crashed target? I mean, if they live, and hit you back for just 3i then they get to reroll join battle and attack you a second time. If their charms aren't perilous, they are just as dangerous crashed as not.<br /> <br /> Is the answer to Delay so that you can Clash or go after them and get a double turn?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T13:58:55-08:00","id":1348006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347891-when-should-npcs-launch-decisives?p=1347990#post1347990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had been revisiting the implications and strategies of when to go for Decisive Attacks recently as well, prompted by a comment in the other thread about a couple Buck-Ogres being more challenging if you are already at -2.<br /> <br /> At what point is the risk of suffering Initiative Shift worth the reward on completing a Decisive Attack against a crashed target? I mean, if they live, and hit you back for just 3i then they get to reroll join battle and attack you a second time. If their charms aren't perilous, they are just as dangerous crashed as not.<br /> <br /> Is the answer to Delay so that you can Clash or go after them and get a double turn?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the game.<br /> <br /> Clashing is a fantastic idea, but it's your Decisive against their Wither. So...<br /> <br /> Delaying to go at the bottom of the round could work, but you've got to be prompt if you expect that to work -- remember they're going to reset to Base in three turns. And it's costing you two dice of damage -- more if they successfully Wither you.<br /> <br /> If they're not Crashed, you can hope they Crash you and you Shift (I've done this in play).<br /> <br /> Otherwise, you want to either put them out of the fight with your Decisive, or be able to stack enough Penalties (Wound or otherwise) to make them unable to effectively fight back.<br /> <br /> And, of course, your and their allies have options like Defend Other, launching their own attacks and so forth. And Charms and other weirdness.<br /> <br /> Chances are, they'll have some kind of Perilous effect, even if it's just Hardness. And do you want to bet that they don't? Do you really want to risk your Decisive whiffing on something like The Tower Still Stands? (See the Ahlat vs Octavian fight if you're unconvinced of the benefits of Crashing an opponent before you unleash.)<br /> <br /> Plus there's a load of Charms that work better on Crashed opponents. Not everyone is going to have them, and if you don't then this isn't a factor. But if you do, they're usually worth setting up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-13-2019, 03:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T14:33:38-08:00","id":1348016,"title":"","content":"I think setting a hard cap on init is a bad way to do things. <br /> I think this because it doesn't change the dynamic. The players who want to build to super-init will still build to the cap and unleash from there to minimize the number of decisives they have to use. If the cap is high, 1HKs remain viable. If the cap is low, really lucky witherings are diminished. <br /> <br /> Instead, I'd propose eliminating the 1HK. For example, make Exalted Healing provide the side benefit that the first time in a fight a -2 or -4 health level is damaged, the rest of the damage from that attack is negated. That way, a 3HK is the absolute best you can accomplish against a meaningful foe, so players (and NPCs) are incentivized to get just enough init instead of giant piles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T14:52:12-08:00","id":1348022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347891-when-should-npcs-launch-decisives?p=1348006#post1348006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the game.<br /> <br /> Clashing is a fantastic idea, but it's your Decisive against their Wither. So...<br /> <br /> Delaying to go at the bottom of the round could work, but you've got to be prompt if you expect that to work -- remember they're going to reset to Base in three turns. And it's costing you two dice of damage -- more if they successfully Wither you.<br /> <br /> If they're not Crashed, you can hope they Crash you and you Shift (I've done this in play).<br /> <br /> Otherwise, you want to either put them out of the fight with your Decisive, or be able to stack enough Penalties (Wound or otherwise) to make them unable to effectively fight back.<br /> <br /> And, of course, your and their allies have options like Defend Other, launching their own attacks and so forth. And Charms and other weirdness.<br /> <br /> Chances are, they'll have some kind of Perilous effect, even if it's just Hardness. And do you want to bet that they don't? Do you really want to risk your Decisive whiffing on something like The Tower Still Stands? (See the Ahlat vs Octavian fight if you're unconvinced of the benefits of Crashing an opponent before you unleash.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the validation. I guess there are just more perilous charms than I remember then.<br /> <br /> To help me re-intuit expected damage, I threw together a quick AnyDice function for a withering attack.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://anydice.com/program/188c5\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://anydice.com/anydice-banner.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://anydice.com/program/188c5\" target=\"_blank\"> AnyDice </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://anydice.com/program/188c5\" target=\"_blank\"> https://anydice.com/program/188c5 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> AnyDice is an advanced dice probability calculator, available online. It is created with roleplaying games in mind. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I started off without charms using mirrored characters with 4 dots in relevant stats and mundane medium equipment. If you are able to put a -2 on your opponent their chance of doing at least 3i drops from 29.05% to 17.1%.<br /> <br /> While that -2 is a decent advantage at that level, it will get less and less impactful as attack pools increase, unless your Defense and Soak keeps up.<br /> <br /> edit: decided to change those 4 dot medium mortal into 4 dot medium Solars, and at least 3i goes from 31.09% to 21.28%.<br /> Sometimes I think the Solar excellency is just too good. It warps everything else around it.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://anydice.com/program/188ca\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://anydice.com/anydice-banner.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://anydice.com/program/188ca\" target=\"_blank\"> AnyDice </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://anydice.com/program/188ca\" target=\"_blank\"> https://anydice.com/program/188ca </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> AnyDice is an advanced dice probability calculator, available online. It is created with roleplaying games in mind. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":1542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","user":"MoroseMorgan","date":". 11-12-2019, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T15:46:05-08:00","id":1348030,"title":"","content":"There might be too many variables to say.<br /> <br /> A lot of enemies retreat in their -2s, so putting them there might just see them off. If you have a friend nearby who's also in threatening position then if you flub they can cover you and finish them. Some berzerk creatures actually add their wound penalties to attacks, rather than subtract them, or don't suffer them to their defense at all. You might also just be opening yourself up to their allies, even if they're not likely to hit you at their -2s someone else might be.<br /> <br /> In general getting shifted on is about the worst thing that can happen to you, it all but guarantees that they'll get three attacks in a row, as they get their full join battle, or better, and another attack on top which can be another withering to push them even further. Unlike the ST controlled characters just doing some damage and then dying also isn't really a great option. On the other hand you're a Solar and the game is kind of designed around the idea that a Solar using their full excellency will almost always succeed at whatever action they take, so if you mess up and they try to punish you for it just throttle up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T16:36:08-08:00","id":1348051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347891-when-should-npcs-launch-decisives?p=1347972#post1347972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry because I feel like we are basically on the same line &quot;I want my players not to stack a ton of initiative&quot;, but I feel like you are contesting me but I don't know on what point specifically.<br /> <br /> I think (a) &quot;Staying at max initiative for too many rounds will make you lose initiative&quot; is a solution to players stacking too much initiative, but I'm unsure if I prefer it to (b) &quot;You can't withering at max initiative&quot;. I think (b) is more elegant.</div> </div> </div> </div>We do agree on the not stacking of initiative, but the specific point we're disagreeing on is that you want them to stop them from withering attacks completely once they hit a certain point, while I want to remove the primary benefit of withering attacks but still allow the option. I don't agree with removing an option from the players. I don't presume to know your players, but I expect it's why you got such a kickback from your players on it. Nobody likes having an option taken away for being successful.<br /> <br /> I was thinking on this subject more, about what to do when a player hits the hypothetical max initiative,or even before, to encourage using decisive attacks, and I hit upon the idea of rewarding them for making a decisive. Not just in the damage they get to deal, but to reward them for taking the risk of reverting to base. What rewards would be viable, I'm not sure about. 2-3m per damage dealt? Dealing 5 or more nets 1wp? Revert to (3+damage dealt)i?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T17:09:16-08:00","id":1348070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347891-when-should-npcs-launch-decisives?p=1348051#post1348051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hit upon the idea of rewarding them for making a decisive. Not just in the damage they get to deal, but to reward them for taking the risk of reverting to base.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm confused here. Why isn't &quot;Move towards winning the fight&quot; a reward? Why isn't it enough? I don't mean to sound condescending here, but have you spoken with your players and asked why they're doing the things they're doing? <br /> <br /> If the issue for your players is the risk, then encourage them to cooperate. Coordinating strikes so everybody simultaneously blasts all the enemies into -2s or worse removes some risk. Disengaging to Short before launching a ranged Decisive while your comrades block enemy movement removes a lot of risk. A Defend Other on the guy who's about to Decisive removes most of the risk, even if it's just some shmuck Elite Soldier doing the defending. Unassailable Guardian Posture is the holy grail of risk removal. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T17:11:34-08:00","id":1348072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347891-when-should-npcs-launch-decisives?p=1348070#post1348070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm confused here. Why isn't &quot;Move towards winning the fight&quot; a reward? Why isn't it enough? I don't mean to sound condescending here, but have you spoken with your players and asked why they're doing the things they're doing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they judge the risk of initiative crash to not be worth doing damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T17:54:10-08:00","id":1348087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347891-when-should-npcs-launch-decisives?p=1348072#post1348072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because they judge the risk of initiative crash to not be worth doing damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, but <i>why</i>? Crash isn't in and of itself that bad. Hardness and some charms turn off, an enemy gets 5i. Not that big of a deal if you're not alone, easy enough for an ally to fix with a Withering. Where's this perceived risk coming from? <br /> Has every enemy who got Crashed died soon after, so your players learned that Crash = Death? Was there 'that one moment' where somebody in an advantageous position Decisive'd, got Crashed, and died like a bitch? Are your players just afraid of Crash because it's the bad state? Have the GM or the players been focusing on Crashed characters with Decisives? Has past narration painted Crashed characters as uncool and these guys want their characters to be cool? Are your players terrified of taking damage since the campaign is so fast-paced that a -1 will last for months of real time? The players are going to have some reason for acting the way they do. <br /> You have to know the cause to treat the undesired behavior. If your players think Crash equates to getting focus fired with Decisives, then a WP reward won't work as an incentive since it doesn't help with getting focus fired with Decisives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T19:01:59-08:00","id":1348103,"title":"","content":"Crash really isn't that bad. I had a player who's strategy against mortals was to let them hit his character until he crashed and then let them keep doing that to him until he recovered from the crash than use just that little bit of Initiative he got from to use Heaven Thunder Hammer to launch his target and usually 1-shot them.<br /> <br /> Even if you don't have cool ways to respond to being crashed, simply allowing a character to waste withering attacks on a crashed player is an effective defense for the rest of the party.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T00:52:53-08:00","id":1348183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347891-when-should-npcs-launch-decisives?p=1348016#post1348016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think setting a hard cap on init is a bad way to do things. <br /> I think this because it doesn't change the dynamic. The players who want to build to super-init will still build to the cap and unleash from there to minimize the number of decisives they have to use. If the cap is high, 1HKs remain viable. If the cap is low, really lucky witherings are diminished. <br /> <br /> Instead, I'd propose eliminating the 1HK. For example, make Exalted Healing provide the side benefit that the first time in a fight a -2 or -4 health level is damaged, the rest of the damage from that attack is negated. That way, a 3HK is the absolute best you can accomplish against a meaningful foe, so players (and NPCs) are incentivized to get just enough init instead of giant piles.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd massively incentivise Penalty builds that way. Pain Tolerance becomes an Auto-Buy. The Thrown Charms that stack penalties go from Good to Essential. And you get weird lopsidedness from Melee characters throwing up Five Fold and fighting through at full effectiveness as everyone else bobs up and down with penalties.<br /> <br /> Plus, Hardness just got AWESOME. If you didn't have a reason to take Mela's Coil before!<br /> <br /> Some weird interaction with OBT where the tougher you are the less tough you are.<br /> <br /> And Octavian weeps hysterically over the Tower Still Stands. &quot;My beautiful boy!&quot;<br /> <br /> Personally, I think the current dymanic is great, and I'm going to resist any attempt to fix it. But this is particularly egregious to me. If it works at your table, great -- have fun with it.<br /> <br /> For me, Decisives are meant to be fight enders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T03:28:53-08:00","id":1348202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347891-when-should-npcs-launch-decisives?p=1348183#post1348183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, Decisives are meant to be fight enders.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is how I prefer to do it myself in play, but I spread a little more over npcs and certain builds. A lucky stab right away increases tension if the PCs can't trounce the now-based enemy.<br /> <br /> Dirty Trickers tend to enjoy opening decisives as well. Get some poisons, joint-wounds and the like right away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 11-13-2019, 06:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T04:27:58-08:00","id":1348213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347891-when-should-npcs-launch-decisives?p=1348087#post1348087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, but <i>why</i>? Crash isn't in and of itself that bad. Hardness and some charms turn off, an enemy gets 5i. Not that big of a deal if you're not alone, easy enough for an ally to fix with a Withering. Where's this perceived risk coming from?</div> </div> </div> </div>Initiative Shift, I think, and the thought of an enemy getting an extra swing at you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T04:51:32-08:00","id":1348226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347891-when-should-npcs-launch-decisives?p=1348051#post1348051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We do agree on the not stacking of initiative, but the specific point we're disagreeing on is that you want them to stop them from withering attacks completely once they hit a certain point, while I want to remove the primary benefit of withering attacks but still allow the option. I don't agree with removing an option from the players. I don't presume to know your players, but I expect it's why you got such a kickback from your players on it. Nobody likes having an option taken away for being successful.<br /> <br /> I was thinking on this subject more, about what to do when a player hits the hypothetical max initiative,or even before, to encourage using decisive attacks, and I hit upon the idea of rewarding them for making a decisive. Not just in the damage they get to deal, but to reward them for taking the risk of reverting to base. What rewards would be viable, I'm not sure about. 2-3m per damage dealt? Dealing 5 or more nets 1wp? Revert to (3+damage dealt)i?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll present things from my perspective, which is basically an analogy. You're totally free to disagree with the analogy itself or its content, it's really my point of view.<br /> <br /> The Social System is a subsystem that helps represents the social dynamic in Exalted. It's presented as an abstraction of what the characters wants, how it can be used to make them act and conversely to protect themselves from influence. But the system is an abstraction, its purpose is to represent the dynamic of what happens in the game. There are of course strategies to accomplish your social goals through the mini-game that is the Social System, but at the end of the day, the mini game is supposed to serve the story and the dynamic of the play. For these reasons, let's suppose there is an optimal play which is to have no Intimacy whatsoever, this way no one can influence you to act against anything. You still can do things you care for, but they are not abstracted as intimacies on your character sheet so you actually have an optimal mechanical play. This of course would be terrible, even if I understand any player going for this play style when it is optimal, but that's not what the mini-game wants to emulate.<br /> <br /> That is exactly the way I see a player with total initiative domination still withering during the fight. I understand the optimal logic that is behind, but to me it puts the focus on the abstraction mini-game when the mini-game is supposed to be here to actually help the dynamic of the scene through reversals and back-and-forth play style.<br /> <br /> Also, I would not consider giving a reward to the player for engaging the rules, at least not reward of this &quot;mechanical kind&quot;. If I wanted this kind of mechanic, I would prefer things that advances the plot like &quot;When you decisive damage someone, you can discover one of its Ties through the heat of battle&quot;. I mean I wouldn't add this rule specifically because there are certainly Charms for that, but I would prefer the story be the reward that another abstraction pool increase be the reward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T05:05:21-08:00","id":1348230,"title":"","content":"But that's supported RAW.<br /> <br /> You could use the rules for: Trivial Opponents on page 208; Shenanigans on 194; defeating Crashed characters on 193; or, my personal favorite, &quot;When no enemies remain to offer resistance, the battle<br /> is over&quot; -- if the PCs might lose because of a Decisive attack, then Withering is the logical thing to do, if they so utterly dominate that they can't lose, then relieve your frustration, use the rules as written and announce they have won.<br /> <br /> If the PCs won't kill their meals, take the oppertunity to have Crashed foes run away or beg for their lives. If the PCs have so much Initative and are so clearly winning the fight, running away and hiding seems like the logical thing to do.<br /> <br /> To use the social abstraction, if I want someone to do a life-changing task, I need to use a Defining Intimacy. Getting loads of Initative is getting that Intimacy. But they can still say &quot;no&quot; and spend a Willpower. Keeping on Withering is me degrading the Decision Point Intimacies down to Major so I know my social influence will be accepted. If that's not neccessary, then just letting me succeed would go down better than houseruling that I can't improve my odds.<br /> <br /> Just my two cents. I don't know your players -- maybe that'd cause problems for you?<br /> <br /> (If you actually want the PCs to lose, then use tougher foes so they can't get such untouchable Initative scores.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-13-2019, 08:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T08:52:47-08:00","id":1348272,"title":"","content":"I know these rules and I use these pretty often when the fight is &quot;basically over and nothing's gonna change anyway&quot;, I'm fine with it. I won't really argue anymore because I already stated my point. I understand that other people do not share it, or not in the same way I feel it, I just think I've only seen so few reversals and unexpected returns in Exalted, and generally much more one sided fights and I'm a bit disappointed because I thought it would be a more important part of the experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T10:35:29-08:00","id":1348294,"title":"","content":"It also sounds like if someone is able to effectively hoard initiative then their ability to gain it and hold on to it has outpaced their competition. Making it too difficult for them to gain initiative is less fun, but if opposition is equally able to steal initiative, and the numbers fluctuate back and forth more, people would be more keen to use it while they have it. Health Tracks growing with the other competencies would also help, if you can make it less and less feasible to be 1HKO'd with the init score they can maintain, it becomes more necessary to have multiple successful decisive attacks.<br /> <br /> Would changing the Crash Reset to 2 rounds provide the desired incentive? You already can't get an Initiative Break bonus if the target just came out of crash, or the following round.<br /> <br /> It also seems like the threat of Initiative Shift has a real warping effect. Either Base Initiative, standard health levels, and hardness needs to be higher, or expected withering damage needs to stay smaller as things scale. Also having some of these break points laid out in plain language might help new storytellers/players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T11:04:27-08:00","id":1348302,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not sure I understand why hoarding initiative is bad, unless you\u2019ve got big multiattacks all you can do with it is destroy one enemy with a big initiative pool, and depending on the enemy that might take a huge amount. Boar-tusk crocodiles need, on average, a 38 initiative attack to die, and that\u2019s just on average, 50% of the time a 38i attack won\u2019t kill it. Even if they\u2019re not being compelled to stay, you still need about 25i to drive them off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T11:10:34-08:00","id":1348304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347891-when-should-npcs-launch-decisives?p=1348294#post1348294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also sounds like if someone is able to effectively hoard initiative then their ability to gain it and hold on to it has outpaced their competition. Making it too difficult for them to gain initiative is less fun, but if opposition is equally able to steal initiative, and the numbers fluctuate back and forth more, people would be more keen to use it while they have it. Health Tracks growing with the other competencies would also help, if you can make it less and less feasible to be 1HKO'd with the init score they can maintain, it becomes more necessary to have multiple successful decisive attacks.<br /> <br /> Would changing the Crash Reset to 2 rounds provide the desired incentive? You already can't get an Initiative Break bonus if the target just came out of crash, or the following round.<br /> <br /> It also seems like the threat of Initiative Shift has a real warping effect. Either Base Initiative, standard health levels, and hardness needs to be higher, or expected withering damage needs to stay smaller as things scale. Also having some of these break points laid out in plain language might help new storytellers/players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I like the status quo.<br /> <br /> If you make Withering damage smaller or Base Initative higher, you still don't see dramatic reversals of fortune.<br /> <br /> Make Hardness higher and you encourage Initative hoarding.<br /> <br /> Health levels doesn't change healing time -- PCs don't want to get hit.<br /> <br /> Crash reset might work.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> Chausse, I feel your frustration but that's exactly what your Initative hoarding PCs don't want. If they're winning, they don't want a dramatic reversal of fortune. If you want to change their behaviour, I suggest talking with them and explaining why the game is better if they suddenly go from winning to losing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T11:46:55-08:00","id":1348314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347891-when-should-npcs-launch-decisives?p=1348304#post1348304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, I like the status quo.<br /> <br /> If you make Withering damage smaller or Base Initative higher, you still don't see dramatic reversals of fortune.<br /> <br /> Make Hardness higher and you encourage Initative hoarding.<br /> <br /> Health levels doesn't change healing time -- PCs don't want to get hit.<br /> <br /> Crash reset might work.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> Chausse, I feel your frustration but that's exactly what your Initative hoarding PCs don't want. If they're winning, they don't want a dramatic reversal of fortune. If you want to change their behaviour, I suggest talking with them and explaining why the game is better if they suddenly go from winning to losing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry if my phrasing was ambiguous. I wasn't trying to change Withering values necessarily, but making sure people focus on Soak as much as they do Attack/Defense so that expected damage stays the same as all values increase. Sometimes it just takes longer to internalize that Soak actually matters this edition.<br /> I was also talking about increasing Base Initiative and Hardness in tandem so that we don't have such a narrow needle of 3i to thread. Since Base Initiative is (almost) universally 3i, everything else has to spin around it. The problem is that Base Initiative being the number that keeps you out of crash or being Shifted is also your potential spam attack damage. I mentioned health levels because if spam damage goes up it could also potentially compensate, which probably just confused the whole thing more. Sorry.<br /> <br /> I think I'm fine with what people usually come to as their status quo from my limited and rusty experience combined with the anecdotal evidence I see, but it also sounds like some people defer to being overly cautious. I also think this inflated caution comes from people not necessarily being able to easily anticipate expected damage due to all of the variables involved. Being at base initiative with the looming threat of crash and or Initiative shift is only as likely as someone dealing 3i, but unless you've played enough to get a feel for expected damage you don't really know.<br /> <br /> For a parallel example of what I'm walking through again, I recently got into playing 40k, and when I first started I was looking at unit options and couldn't intuit the value of Toughness 4 versus Toughness 5 on it's own, until I started to see what the availability and cost of my oppositions Strength 4+ was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T12:28:48-08:00","id":1348318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347891-when-should-npcs-launch-decisives?p=1348314#post1348314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry if my phrasing was ambiguous. I wasn't trying to change Withering values necessarily, but making sure people focus on Soak as much as they do Attack/Defense so that expected damage stays the same as all values increase.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this depends a lot on what enemies you\u2019re facing and how much your players can avoid the temptation to just max their combat stat. A Solar who\u2019s not really trying that hard can very easily get a defense value of 10-12, at which point the only things in the game that stand any real chance of hitting them are second circle demons or their equivalents, or other exalted. Even otherwise powerful gods and elementals don\u2019t stand a chance, especially if you can put them into their -2s. I\u2019m talking like less than one tenth of one percent of a chance to hit you here. Conversely, almost no enemy has a defense above 5, so your attack doesn\u2019t matter nearly as much as your damage against those kinds of foes. If you want to play it really safe and boring you just need to excellency your defense all the time and attack with nothing.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s boring and it takes a long time, but to be fair that is kind of what overly cautious gameplay is like. <br /> <br /> Against really high skill enemies like other exalted it can kind of shift the other way. If your enemy can throw 29 dice into an attack roll against you, then boosting your defense is almost pointless compared to boosting your soak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T12:32:50-08:00","id":1348319,"title":"","content":"Right. But if you make it harder to Shift/Crash people after Decisives, then there's no dramatic reversal of fortunes. The people who were winning prior to launching the Decisives will continue to be winning after the Decisives, and the people who were losing don't get a chance to pull things back. Which is really no different to just launching Withering attacks all the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T12:57:44-08:00","id":1348320,"title":"","content":"Epiphany (probably the second time I've had this over the years)- the dramatic reversal of fortunes has nothing to do with Decisives, they really are supposed to be the fight enders with the risky alternative being the frequent low init attack. The dynamic nature of Ex3 combat comes from Withering favoring the attackers, and if you and your opponents aren't trading blows, then it will be pretty static.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T23:15:10-08:00","id":1348415,"title":"","content":"I got a bit too into this question and decided to write a program to run preposterous quantities of 1v1 fights to assess the impact of different &quot;When to Decisive&quot; mindsets. Right now it's running* bar brawls between Elite Soldier level combatants. <br /> Current results indicate that, in a fight between a guy who refuses to Decisive until his opponent is in crash and he has 3x as much initiative as his opponent has health and a guy who just throws a decisive the second he's got double-digit initiative, the latter wins ~80% of the time. This suggests that the combat system discourages caution. <br /> <br /> *: DISCLAIMER: The program has been debugged to the point of running. Not &quot;Running correctly&quot;, not &quot;Running and seems to be correct&quot;, just &quot;Gives Output&quot;. Zero real testing has occurred yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T01:44:50-08:00","id":1348440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347891-when-should-npcs-launch-decisives?p=1348304#post1348304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chausse, I feel your frustration but that's exactly what your Initative hoarding PCs don't want. If they're winning, they don't want a dramatic reversal of fortune. If you want to change their behaviour, I suggest talking with them and explaining why the game is better if they suddenly go from winning to losing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know exactly what you mean by &quot;lose&quot;, but I don't think that's my point. I want to have a bit more surprises to some things, like combat movement, decision to flee, etc ... can come a bit more as a surprise and be less a &quot;prepared battle plan&quot;.<br /> <br /> For example, right now, the almost only thing I did that successfully made players move and create more dynamic and unplanned execution is when my NPC's basically have &quot;WoW boss powers&quot;, ie be careful because next turn there will be an explosion there, or you are targeted by a big attack coming next round maybe you should hide, but they don't feel really &quot;natural&quot; solutions and I'd like to improve this feeling, and also make it possible for them to come from the players.<br /> <br /> I obviously don't think I'm a perfect game designer, and I don't like talking it here because it makes me feel like I'm bragging which I don't want to, but an example of things that have a core idea that I like is one of the &quot;Charms/moves&quot; I made up in the home brew battle thread :<ul><li>NPC target a spot on the battlefield</li> <li>He gains increased defense while he is travelling toward the spot with soldiers.</li> <li>The defense bonus stop if the players can somehow make the travel impossible.</li> </ul>And this allows the players to solve a &quot;combat problem&quot; with unexpected answers and maybe have some reversals (take out the soldiers, block the way, etc ...). And I really thought the base Combat System would provide this &quot;on its own&quot;, through simple use, but for the moment it appears to me it's not the case and I'm looking for tools and ideas that allows me to create simply this kind of feeling, because the only time I could do this it took me way too hours to design NPCs, powers, stakes and stuff to feel like a really a cool action scene.<br /> <br /> So I know I'm renting and going kinda far from the discussion so I'm sorry I guess we could as well call it a day since many solutions and ideas were proposed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":24291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","user":"Chausse","date":". 11-14-2019, 05:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T01:47:19-08:00","id":1348441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347891-when-should-npcs-launch-decisives?p=1348415#post1348415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got a bit too into this question and decided to write a program to run preposterous quantities of 1v1 fights to assess the impact of different &quot;When to Decisive&quot; mindsets. Right now it's running* bar brawls between Elite Soldier level combatants. <br /> Current results indicate that, in a fight between a guy who refuses to Decisive until his opponent is in crash and he has 3x as much initiative as his opponent has health and a guy who just throws a decisive the second he's got double-digit initiative, the latter wins ~80% of the time. This suggests that the combat system discourages caution. <br /> <br /> *: DISCLAIMER: The program has been debugged to the point of running. Not &quot;Running correctly&quot;, not &quot;Running and seems to be correct&quot;, just &quot;Gives Output&quot;. Zero real testing has occurred yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you factor in the hot mess which is Actual Play. Because it won't be one-on-one with evenly matched foes. There will be Charms that cancel wound penalties. Charms that raise Hardness. Charms that can only be used on Decisives. Charms which stack additional penalities. People run away. Reinforcements arrive at dramatic moments.<br /> <br /> Death by a thousand cuts is a great strategy (especially paired with Solar Thrown and the like). But you're comparing combatants with no Perilous Charms, no Hardness, no Join Battle boosters... fighting under conditions that almost never occur in play. (Would love to see the code though.)<br /> <br /> I'm encouraged. I've nothing against seeing people gambling on their attacks, wearing their foes down. And if people knew that playing less conservatively means they're more likely to win, then I think that addresses the main concerns of people looking to change the system.<br /> <br /> But I'm not confident that your experiment has ecological validity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T07:36:36-08:00","id":1348478,"title":"","content":"Depending on the foe you\u2019re facing holding on to initiative for too long is also a gamble. There shouldn\u2019t ever really be an exalted combat where your group isn\u2019t losing motes every turn, so if you hold out for another five turns farming up more and more initiative you\u2019re likely to just run dry on your mote pool. That would mean that either you finish off the fight with the last of your motes and are now a sitting duck for anything else that happens for the next hour or two, or you start fighting a much more fair fight with just your regen motes, and then at the end you\u2019re still a sitting duck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T12:28:19-08:00","id":1348700,"title":"","content":"If you want to change up the balance of combat a bit so a crashed target isn't as out of the fight, one option is to give them a bonus that helps with turning the tide - something like doubling mote regen while crashed.<br /> <br /> This has very definite knock-on effects, but may make players less paranoid about running the risk of resetting initiative and being crashed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13112-kenlon","name":"kenlon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}